    <div class="eyebrow">ABOUT / PRODUCT PRACTICE</div>
    <h1>Every product judgment<br />should face real use.</h1>
    <p class="dek">Hi, I’m tinylion1024. I work across product, AI delivery, and growth—and keep testing those judgments in real products.</p>
    <div class="essay-rule"></div>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>I care about one question: how can product judgment, AI delivery, and growth validation work as one loop that turns an idea into something people actually use?</p>
      <p>Product judgment chooses what deserves to exist, AI shortens the path to delivery, and growth tests that judgment against real behavior. Tools and process should serve that loop, not become the story.</p>
      <p>This site is not a résumé or a feed. It is where I document product decisions, AI building workflows, growth experiments, and the conclusions that survive practice.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="principles" aria-label="My working principles">
      <div><span>01 / JUDGE</span><p>Decide what not to build.</p></div>
      <div><span>02 / BUILD</span><p>Use AI to shorten the distance from idea to product.</p></div>
      <div><span>03 / VERIFY</span><p>Test judgment against real use and growth.</p></div>
    </div>
    <section class="beliefs" aria-labelledby="beliefs-title">
      <span class="eyebrow">WHAT I BELIEVE</span>
      <h2 id="beliefs-title">Four beliefs I keep testing</h2>
      <ol>
        <li><strong>A product is not a feature list.</strong> It is a set of validated trade-offs.</li>
        <li><strong>Models are infrastructure.</strong> The delivery system determines whether AI creates value.</li>
        <li><strong>Growth is not a traffic trick.</strong> It is the result of value being repeatedly used and shared.</li>
        <li><strong>Tools and process are not the product.</strong> They should make the right work easier to do.</li>
      </ol>
    </section>
